 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# 02 — Customer Segmentation: RFM & KMeans Clustering\n\nThis notebook segments customers into actionable groups using:\n1. **RFM Analysis** — rule-based segmentation\n2. **KMeans Clustering** — data-driven behavioural clusters",
   "id": "md_#_02_—_C"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "import sys, warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\nsys.path.insert(0, '..')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.ticker as mtick\nimport seaborn as sns\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom src.data_loader           import DataLoader\nfrom src.data_cleaner          import DataCleaner\nfrom src.feature_engineering   import FeatureEngineer\nfrom src.customer_segmentation import CustomerSegmentation\n\nsns.set_theme(style='darkgrid', palette='husl')\nplt.rcParams.update({'figure.dpi': 120, 'font.size': 11,\n                     'axes.titlesize': 13, 'axes.titleweight': 'bold'})\nVISUALS = Path('../visuals')\nVISUALS.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n\nloader  = DataLoader()\ndf_raw  = loader.load_raw_data()\ncleaner = DataCleaner()\ndf      = cleaner.clean(df_raw)\nprint(\"Data loaded:\", df.shape)",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_import_s"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. RFM Analysis\n\n**Recency (R):** How recently did the customer purchase?\n**Frequency (F):** How often do they purchase?\n**Monetary (M):** How much do they spend?\n\nEach metric is scored 1–5 using quintiles; combined RFM Score = R + F + M (range 3–15).",
   "id": "md_##_1._RF"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "fe  = FeatureEngineer()\nrfm = fe.compute_rfm_scores(df)\nprint(rfm.describe())\nrfm.head()",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_fe__=_Fe"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 5))\ncolors = ['#00d4ff', '#7c3aed', '#22c55e']\nfor ax, col, label, c in zip(axes,\n                               ['recency', 'frequency', 'monetary'],\n                               ['Recency (days)', 'Frequency (orders)', 'Monetary (INR)'],\n                               colors):\n    ax.hist(rfm[col], bins=30, color=c, edgecolor='white', alpha=0.85)\n    ax.set_title(f'{label} Distribution')\n    ax.set_xlabel(label)\n    ax.set_ylabel('Customers')\nplt.suptitle('RFM Score Distributions', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(VISUALS / 'rfm_distributions.png', bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_fig,_axe"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Customer Segments",
   "id": "md_##_2._Cu"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "cust_feat = fe.build_customer_features(df)\nseg       = CustomerSegmentation()\ncust_feat = seg.rfm_segmentation(cust_feat)\nsegment_counts = cust_feat['rfm_segment'].value_counts()\nprint(segment_counts)",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_cust_fea"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "SEGMENT_COLORS = {\n    'Champions'          : '#22c55e',\n    'Loyal Customers'    : '#00d4ff',\n    'Potential Loyalists': '#7c3aed',\n    'Promising'          : '#f59e0b',\n    'New Customers'      : '#06b6d4',\n    'At Risk'            : '#ef4444',\n    'Lost Customers'     : '#9ca3af',\n}\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\nseg_df = segment_counts.reset_index()\nseg_df.columns = ['segment', 'count']\ncolors_list = [SEGMENT_COLORS.get(s, '#888') for s in seg_df['segment']]\n\nseg_df.sort_values('count', ascending=True).plot(\n    kind='barh', x='segment', y='count', ax=axes[0],\n    color=colors_list, legend=False)\naxes[0].set_title('Customer Segment Distribution')\naxes[0].set_xlabel('Number of Customers')\n\naxes[1].pie(seg_df['count'], labels=seg_df['segment'],\n            colors=colors_list, autopct='%1.1f%%', startangle=90,\n            pctdistance=0.75, labeldistance=1.05)\naxes[1].set_title('Segment Share (%)')\n\nplt.suptitle('RFM Customer Segments', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(VISUALS / 'rfm_segments.png', bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\nprint(\"Saved: rfm_segments.png\")",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_SEGMENT_"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Segment Profiles & Business Recommendations",
   "id": "md_##_3._Se"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "profiles = seg.generate_segment_profiles(cust_feat, df)\nprint(profiles[['rfm_segment','size','pct','avg_clv','avg_order_value','avg_orders','recommendation']].to_string(index=False))",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_profiles"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. KMeans Clustering — Elbow Method",
   "id": "md_##_4._KM"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "cust_feat, inertias = seg.behavioral_segmentation(cust_feat)\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\nax.plot(range(1, 9), inertias, 'o-', color='#00d4ff', linewidth=2.5, markersize=8)\nax.axvline(x=4, color='#ef4444', linestyle='--', label='Chosen k=4')\nax.set_title('KMeans Elbow Plot — Choosing Optimal k')\nax.set_xlabel('Number of Clusters (k)')\nax.set_ylabel('Inertia (WCSS)')\nax.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(VISUALS / 'kmeans_elbow.png', bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_cust_fea"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5. Cluster Visualisation (PCA 2D)",
   "id": "md_##_5._Cl"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "CLUSTER_COLORS = {'High Value':'#22c55e','Medium Value':'#00d4ff',\n                  'Budget Shoppers':'#f59e0b','Churned Risk':'#ef4444'}\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 7))\nfor label, grp in cust_feat.groupby('cluster_label'):\n    ax.scatter(grp['pca_x'], grp['pca_y'], label=label,\n               color=CLUSTER_COLORS.get(label, '#888'),\n               alpha=0.6, s=30, edgecolors='none')\nax.set_title('Customer Clusters — PCA 2D Projection')\nax.set_xlabel('Principal Component 1')\nax.set_ylabel('Principal Component 2')\nax.legend(title='Cluster', framealpha=0.8)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(VISUALS / 'cluster_pca.png', bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_CLUSTER_"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 6. Cluster Profiles",
   "id": "md_##_6._Cl"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "cluster_profiles = seg.generate_segment_profiles(cust_feat, df, segment_col='cluster_label')\nprint(cluster_profiles[['cluster_label','size','pct','avg_clv','avg_order_value','avg_orders','recommendation']].to_string(index=False))",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "code_cluster_"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Key Takeaways\n\n- **Champions** (~15%): Highest CLV, most frequent buyers → reward with loyalty perks\n- **At Risk** customers need immediate win-back campaigns with targeted discounts\n- **New Customers** show high recency but low frequency → critical to convert to loyalists\n- KMeans clusters confirm clear separation between high-spend and budget shoppers",
   "id": "md_##_Key_T"
  }
